              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പക — paka — \"a grudge; vengefulness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പഴയ വഴക്കിന്റെ പക അവൻ മറന്നില്ല. paḻaya vaḻakkinṟe paka avan maṟannilla. He did not forget the grudge from the old quarrel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പക (paka) വീട്ടുക is to take revenge, literally to pay off a grudge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പക (paka) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3808 lists it beside verbs for dividing and sharing, with the sense of separation and enmity (DEDR 3808)."
            }
          ]
        },
